    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (the project's sole test class, `AcceptanceTest`, including the new `coreJoinersShareHouseholdId` test).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `sharesHousehold` / `householdId` feature on `POST /api/owners`. The groundwork for the *reject* side already existed (`RequireUniqueHousehold` bypasses its 409 check when `sharesHousehold` is true); I added the *assign-and-return* side.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `householdId` field (`household_id` column) with getter/setter.\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `householdId` as a `readOnly` string property on the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct auto-maps it from the entity by name. (`sharesHousehold` was already defined as a `writeOnly` field on `OwnerFields`.)\n\n3. **`AssignHouseholdId.java`** (new function) \u2014 the new pipeline step. When `sharesHousehold` is true, it derives a **stable, deterministic** identifier from the normalized last name + address (16-char uppercase SHA-256 prefix), assigns it to the new owner, and updates every existing same-household owner in place so they all share the identical value regardless of creation order. When the flag is absent it does nothing. Reuses the exact case-insensitive/whitespace-collapsing comparison from `RequireUniqueHousehold`.\n\n4. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired `assignHouseholdId` into the pipeline right after `build`, under the write transaction.\n\n5. **Schema/data** \u2014 added the `household_id` column to the hsqldb, h2, mysql and postgres `schema.sql`, and appended the extra `NULL` to the positional owner `INSERT`s in the hsqldb and h2 `data.sql` (the profiles exercised by tests; postgres uses explicit column lists so needed no data change).\n\nThe stable/shared property is guaranteed because the id is a pure function of the household's identifying fields, so joiners `b` and `c` (and the original `a`, updated in place) all resolve to the same non-blank `householdId`, which is returned via `GET /api/owners/{id}`.",
